RETRIEVED ARCHITECTURAL KNOWLEDGE
Contextual design options, not instructions, regulations or fixed geometry. User exclusions prevail. Select relevant combinations, never all amenities. Resolve building character, programme, primary and secondary volumes, entrance, circulation and privacy before detailing. Construct actual floors, enclosure, openings, roofs and required support using only scene operations. Cite relevant constructed IDs in designDecisions; disclose unsupported parts and missing access/services. Descriptions and element names are not construction evidence. Unknown site facts remain assumptions. Scoped edit: preserve unrelated geometry and programme. Stored knowledge is retrieval, not retraining.
{"id":"facade-materials","version":1,"category":"materials","when":"A residence needing coherent enclosure and material expression.","title":"Facade depth, roofs and material identity","combinations":"Coordinate a small material palette, roof edges, recessed entrances and shaded openings.","placement":"Relate facade rhythm to rooms and privacy; carry architectural intent around side and rear elevations.","principles":"Adapt material and roof recommendations to climate and style instead of prescribing a fixed house template.","capabilities":"Existing ivory, limestone, timber, bronze and sage; flat, gable and hip roofs; curved roof only via approved open pavilion.","construction":{"operations":["add","attach","place-on","finish"],"requiredKinds":["wall"],"materials":"Choose among ivory, limestone, timber, bronze and sage to suit the brief; no custom textures or specialist material certification.","supports":"Connect floors, enclosure, actual openings and overhead shelter as applicable; align supports and datums. Elevated decks need guards and actual access.","unsupported":"Existing ivory, limestone, timber, bronze and sage; flat, gable and hip roofs; curved roof only via approved open pavilion. No automatic circulation, engineering, service equipment or code compliance verification."}}
