{"id":"roof-main-secondary","version":1,"category":"roof-outdoor","when":"Use when the brief or chosen programme calls for primary and secondary roof hierarchy.","title":"Primary and secondary roof hierarchy","combinations":"Timber deck and ivory or limestone roof edges; guards may use the balcony glass primitive.","placement":"Give the principal occupied volume a clear roof and set lower roofs over subordinate spaces.","principles":"Do not let lower roofs intersect upper room windows.","capabilities":"Use direct-scene primitives: plate, roof. No automatic stairs, waterproofing, drainage, roof loading or guard compliance certification.","construction":{"operations":["add","attach","place-on","finish"],"requiredKinds":["plate","roof"],"materials":"Timber deck and ivory or limestone roof edges; guards may use the balcony glass primitive.","supports":"Support elevated decks with walls or posts, guard exposed edges, provide actual door access and supported shade.","unsupported":"No automatic stairs, waterproofing, drainage, roof loading or guard compliance certification."}}
{"id":"waterfront-estate","version":1,"category":"climate-site","when":"Sites with a stated water edge or coastal view.","title":"Waterfront privacy and site sequence","combinations":"Consider view terraces and pools; docks only with suitable water access, brief and permissions.","placement":"Protect the public shore edge and setbacks; place living towards views, private suites away from public routes, vehicle arrival landward when feasible.","principles":"Do not invent a surveyed shore, flood elevation or legal setback; keep site assumptions explicit.","capabilities":"Flat site composition and water surfaces are available; no coastal terrain, flood simulation or marine engineering.","construction":{"operations":["add","attach","place-on","finish"],"requiredKinds":["plate","wall","roof"],"materials":"Choose among ivory, limestone, timber, bronze and sage to suit the brief; no custom textures or specialist material certification.","supports":"Connect floors, enclosure, actual openings and overhead shelter as applicable; align supports and datums. Elevated decks need guards and actual access.","unsupported":"Flat site composition and water surfaces are available; no coastal terrain, flood simulation or marine engineering. No automatic circulation, engineering, service equipment or code compliance verification."}}
